Trusted registry public keys

Each key is a file named <keyId>.pub that holds the base64 encoding of the
32 byte raw Ed25519 public key on a single line. Every .pub file in this
directory is embedded in the CLI and trusted to sign the registry index. Keys
can only be added by changing this directory and releasing the CLI. No
environment variable, config entry or flag can add or replace a key.

To rotate a key, embed the new key next to the old one, release the CLI, then
let the signer switch to the new key ID. The old key is removed in a later
release, once the CLI versions that only know the old key are no longer
supported.

No production key is embedded yet, see the TODO in ../keys.go.
